<title>CANADA: Canada's Goodale aims at 3.5 pct world food market.</title>
<headline>Canada's Goodale aims at 3.5 pct world food market.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Agriculture Minister Ralph Goodale said on Saturday his government's objective is to hold a 3.5 percent share of the world's food markets.</p>
<p>&quot;We want to recapture Canada's traditional 3.5 percent share of global agrifood markets by the year 2000 and that means we should exceed US$23 billion dollars' worth in agrifood exports,&quot; Goodale told delegates at the annual Canadian Farm Writers' conference.</p>
<p>Canada exported US$17.5 billion worth of food products in 1995, a 30 percent rise from 1993 export level, he said.</p>
<p>Exports in 1996 may top last year's level by 10 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;So far in 1996, we're close to 10 percent ahead of the pace that we set last year. We're going to reach at least US$20 billion-worth of agrifood trade by the year 2000 but we want to do better than that,&quot; Goodale added.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
